# Lets the mtgkiosk service (running as `admin`) restart itself after pulling an
# update, and shut the appliance down from the UI.
#
# Both grants are for the OUTER `systemd-run`, not for `systemctl`. systemd-run
# in system mode calls StartTransientUnit on the system manager, which polkit
# gates behind auth_admin_keep, and a `User=admin` system service has no login
# session for polkit to prompt. Granting only the inner systemctl - which is all
# this file did until 2026-09-11 - is useless: systemd-run is the first thing
# that needs privilege, so it fails first and the inner command never runs.
#
# sudo matches argv literally and neither line uses a wildcard, so these permit
# exactly two command lines and nothing else. In particular they do NOT permit
# arbitrary `systemd-run`, which would be equivalent to unrestricted root.
#
# src/mtgkiosk/app.py must match these character-for-character;
# tests/test_privileged_commands.py fails if the two ever drift apart.
admin ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemd-run --on-active=2 /usr/bin/systemctl restart mtgkiosk.service
admin ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemd-run --on-active=2 /usr/bin/systemctl poweroff
